# ABP Dependency Injection

## Conventional Registration
ABP automatically registers services by convention. No manual registration needed for:
- Classes implementing `ITransientDependency`, `ISingletonDependency`, or `IScopedDependency`
- Classes inheriting from `ApplicationService`, `DomainService`, `AbpController`, `AbpPageModel`
- Repository implementations inheriting from `BasicRepositoryBase`

## Service Lifetimes
- Use `ITransientDependency` for transient lifetime
- Use `ISingletonDependency` for singleton lifetime  
- Use `IScopedDependency` for scoped lifetime
- Use `[Dependency]` attribute for more control

## Exposing Services
- Use `[ExposeServices(typeof(IMyService))]` to control which interfaces a class exposes
- Use `[ExposeKeyedService<IMyService>("key")]` for keyed service registration
- ABP exposes class itself and default interfaces (matching naming convention) by default

## Property Injection
- ABP supports property injection via Autofac integration
- Set properties as `public` with public setter for optional dependencies
- Always provide a default/fallback value for property-injected services
- Use `[DisablePropertyInjection]` to disable for specific properties or classes

## Cached Service Providers
- Use `ICachedServiceProvider` for optimized service resolution with caching
- Use `ITransientCachedServiceProvider` when cache should not be shared between services
- These avoid memory leaks and improve performance when resolving services multiple times

## Replacing Services
- Use `[Dependency(ReplaceServices = true)]` attribute
- Or use `context.Services.Replace(ServiceDescriptor.Transient<IService, MyService>())`
